---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const privacySupportEmail = "support@updates.houseofrosefl.com";
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="House of Rose LLC privacy policy, data sharing practices, and messaging terms and conditions."
>
	<section class="bg-charcoal py-24 max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
		<div class="text-center mb-16">
			<p class="text-xs tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-gold mb-4">
				House of Rose LLC
			</p>
			<h1 class="font-serif text-5xl text-white">Privacy Policy</h1>
		</div>

		<div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-white/80">
			<p class="lead text-xl text-white/70 leading-relaxed">
				House of Rose LLC respects your privacy. This policy explains
				how we handle customer information, including information
				connected to SMS messaging.
			</p>

			<h2>Information We Collect</h2>
			<p>
				We may collect information you provide when you contact us,
				request services, book an appointment, subscribe to messaging,
				or communicate with House of Rose LLC. This may include your
				name, contact information, appointment details, preferences, and
				messages you send to us.
			</p>

			<h2>How We Use Information</h2>
			<p>
				We use customer information to answer questions, provide
				support, manage appointments, communicate about services, send
				requested messages, and operate our business.
			</p>

			<h2>Data Sharing</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					• Customer data is not shared with 3rd parties for
					promotional or marketing purposes.
				</li>
				<li>
					• Mobile opt-in and consent are never shared with anyone for
					any purpose. Any information sharing that may be mentioned
					elsewhere in this policy excludes mobile opt-in data.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>House of Rose LLC Messaging Terms and Conditions</h2>
			<ol>
				<li>
					1. The messaging program consists of general conversational
					messaging to answer questions and provide support to
					customers, promotional offers or discounts, any promotion of
					your products/services.
				</li>
				<li>
					2. You can cancel the SMS service at any time. Just text 'STOP'
					to the phone number from which you received messages. After
					you send the SMS message 'STOP' to us, we will send you an
					SMS message to confirm that you have been unsubscribed.
					After this, you will no longer receive SMS messages from us.
					If you want to join again, just sign up as you did the first
					time and we will start sending SMS messages to you again.
				</li>
				<li>
					3. If you are experiencing issues with the messaging program
					you can reply with the keyword HELP for more assistance, or
					you can get help directly at info@houseofrosefl.com.
				</li>
				<li>
					4. Carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages.
				</li>
				<li>
					5. As always, message and data rates may apply for any messages
					sent to you from us and to us from you. Message frequency
					will vary based on communication needs. If you have any
					questions about your text plan or data plan, it is best to
					contact your wireless provider.
				</li>
				<li>
					6. If you have any questions regarding privacy, please read our
					privacy policy contained in the rest of this document/page.
				</li>
			</ol>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				If you have questions about this privacy policy or House of Rose
				LLC messaging, use the privacy support form below. Messages are
				sent from <strong>{privacySupportEmail}</strong>.
			</p>
		</div>

		<form
			id="privacy-contact"
			method="post"
			action="/.netlify/functions/privacy-contact"
			class="mt-12 border border-gold/20 bg-charcoal-light p-6 shadow-sm"
		>
			<div class="mb-6">
				<p class="text-xs tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-gold mb-2">
					Privacy Support
				</p>
				<h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-white">
					Send a Privacy Request
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/70">
					This form is handled through Resend and forwards privacy
					messages to House of Rose at info@houseofrosefl.com.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
				<label class="block">
					<span class="text-xs tracking-widest uppercase text-gold">
						Name
					</span>
					<input
						type="text"
						name="name"
						required
						autocomplete="name"
						class="mt-2 w-full border border-white/10 bg-charcoal px-4 py-3 text-white outline-none focus:border-gold transition-colors"
					/>
				</label>

				<label class="block">
					<span class="text-xs tracking-widest uppercase text-gold">
						Email
					</span>
					<input
						type="email"
						name="email"
						required
						autocomplete="email"
						class="mt-2 w-full border border-white/10 bg-charcoal px-4 py-3 text-white outline-none focus:border-gold transition-colors"
					/>
				</label>
			</div>

			<label class="mt-5 block">
				<span class="text-xs tracking-widest uppercase text-gold">
					Subject
				</span>
				<input
					type="text"
					name="subject"
					required
					class="mt-2 w-full border border-white/10 bg-charcoal px-4 py-3 text-white outline-none focus:border-gold transition-colors"
				/>
			</label>

			<label class="mt-5 block">
				<span class="text-xs tracking-widest uppercase text-gold">
					Message
				</span>
				<textarea
					name="message"
					required
					rows="6"
					class="mt-2 w-full border border-white/10 bg-charcoal px-4 py-3 text-white outline-none focus:border-gold transition-colors"
				></textarea>
			</label>

			<label class="hidden" aria-hidden="true">
				<span>Website</span>
				<input type="text" name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
			</label>

			<div class="mt-6 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
				<p class="text-sm text-white/60">
					Visible sender: {privacySupportEmail}
				</p>
				<button type="submit" class="btn-gold">Send Request</button>
			</div>
		</form>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	/* Override prose heading colors to match brand */
	.prose h2 {
		@apply text-gold font-serif text-2xl mb-4 mt-8;
	}

	/* Ensure proper text contrast */
	.prose p,
	.prose li {
		@apply text-white/80;
	}

	.prose strong {
		@apply text-white;
	}

	/* List styling */
	.prose ul,
	.prose ol {
		@apply text-white/80;
	}
</style>
